# Netlify rewrite rules. Inert on GitHub Pages, which ignores this file.
#
# The whole point: serve index.html for every app route with a 200 status,
# instead of GitHub Pages' 404.html-with-404-status. That is the single thing
# standing between the current setup and /tools/rnaflow being indexable.
#
# 200 = rewrite (URL stays, content served) — not 301, which would bounce
# every deep link back to the home page and lose the path.

# ── Keep repository files out of the published site ──────────────────────
# publish = "." serves the whole repo, so the function source, the build script
# and the internal docs were all downloadable. None of them contain secrets —
# those live in environment variables — but the auth source spells out the rate
# limits, the token format and the exact validation, which is a free head start
# for anyone attacking the gate.
#
# The trailing ! forces these ahead of the static file that would otherwise win.
/netlify/*    /404.html   404!
/tools/build-sitemap.py   /404.html   404!
/HOSTING.md   /404.html   404!
/README.md    /404.html   404!

/tools/*      /index.html   200
/learn/*      /index.html   200
/tools        /index.html   200
/learn        /index.html   200
/download     /index.html   200
/resources    /index.html   200
/contact      /index.html   200

# Anything genuinely missing still gets a real 404 from 404.html.
/*            /404.html     404
